56538	56710	56521	56521	he	393	" Or iver you set up the pole o ' your tent amang us , Mr. Moore , we lived i ' peace and quietness -- yea , I may say , in all loving - kindness . I am not myself an aged person as yet , but I can remember as far back as maybe some twenty year , when hand - labour were encouraged and respected , and no mischief - maker had ventured to introduce these here machines which is so pernicious . Now , I 'm not a cloth - dresser myself , but by trade a tailor . Howsiver , my heart is of a softish nature . I 'm a very feeling man , and when I see my brethren oppressed , like my great namesake of old , I stand up for 'em ; for which intent I this day speak with you face to face , and advises you to part wi ' your infernal machinery , and tak on more hands . "
