72823	72981	73129	73129	she	2439	" is Robert 's mental condition to mine . I think only of him ; he has no room , no leisure , to think of me . The feeling called love is and has been for two years the predominant emotion of my heart -- always there , always awake , always astir . Quite other feelings absorb his reflections and govern his faculties . He is rising now , going to leave the church , for service is over . Will he turn his head towards this pew ? No , not once . He has not one look for me . That is hard . A kind glance would have made me happy till to - morrow . I have not got it ; he would not give it ; he is gone . Strange that grief should now almost choke me , because another human being 's eye has failed to greet mine . "
