213680	213749	212758	212758	he	262	" I look out at some early hour of the day , and see a fine , perfect rainbow , bright with promise , gloriously spanning the beclouded welkin of life . An hour afterwards I look again : half the arch is gone , and the rest is faded . Still later , the stern sky denies that it ever wore so benign a symbol of hope . "
